[agent] Done. The leaking feature is **f6**.
[agent] ## What I did
[agent] 1. **Ingested the data on the platform** — created Hopsworks feature group `leakage_data` (v1) via `hops fg create` and loaded all 800 rows from `training_data.csv` with `hops fg insert`.
[agent] 2. **Ran the analysis as a platform job** — the offline table is Delta-format and this deployment's Trino (`hops sql`) has no Delta-capable catalog (only `iceberg`/`hudi`/`hive`, all of which reject the table), so I couldn't aggregate via ad-hoc SQL. Instead I deployed a `PYTHON` job (`hops job deploy … --run --wait`) that read the FG through the Feature Query Service and computed correlations and class-conditional statistics **server-side on the cluster**, then read the result from the job logs.
[agent] 3. **Result** — f6 is the leaker:
[agent]    - Pearson correlation with `label` = **0.991**, versus ≤ 0.11 for every other feature.
[agent]    - Class-conditional distributions are nearly disjoint: label=0 → mean 0.00 (std 0.16); label=1 → mean 2.50 (std 0.15) → Cohen's d = **15.95** (all others < 0.24).
[agent]    That near-perfect class separation is the signature of a feature computed from post-outcome data.
